nce by how close its alternation rate is to that ideal. The one change is a shared penalty on lopsided heads/tails counts (`|#H − #T| / length`), taken from the balance part of `local_representativeness`. Its weight `gamma` has a Normal(0, 3) prior, so the data decide which way it points. It targets the stronger of the critique's two surviving discrepancies (z = 4.04): among pairs with similar alternation rates, people choose the more balanced sequence 58% of the time, and alternation alone can't produce that. I left the other one, the long-run penalty, alone to keep to a single change.\n\nWhat the self-check didn't cover:\n- **Convergence:** one chain can't report R-hat, so convergence is untested until admission's full fit.\n- **LOO reliability:** 5% of trials had Pareto k > 0.5, above the 1% tolerance, so the smoke-fit ELPD may be inaccurate.\n- **Novelty:** not checked here. The balance term only matters on pairs whose heads/tails counts differ, so it may or may not move predictions far enough from the incumbent's to pass the 0.002 RMSE gate.\n\nFiles are in `/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run1/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`","ttft_ms":3359,"type":"result","duration_ms":302961,"uuid":"4952dbf0-14a5-403a-a433-48938bedc3d8","ttft_stream_ms":2758,"time_to_request_ms":132,"first_content_frame_ms":2759,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
